  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. The repo shows that something still reads `channel`, so removing it would break a consumer that's already deployed.\n\n**What I found:**\n- `contracts/consumers/analytics-ingest__OrderPlaced.json` (`deployedVersion: 3`) lists `\"channel\": \"enum:web|store|marketplace\"` as a required field on `OrderPlaced`.\n- `scripts/verify-contracts.mjs` (the ARCH-4 consumer-contract check) checks every `requires` entry. If I drop the field, that check fails with `ARCH-4 FAIL analytics-ingest: OrderPlaced.channel missing`. More importantly, analytics-ingest would stop getting a field it currently depends on.\n- `billing-service` and the `OrderCancelled` contract don't use `channel`, so they're unaffected.\n\n**What the change would cover**, once it's safe to make:\n- `src/core/order.ts`: `CHANNELS`, `Channel`, the `channel` fields on `NewOrder`/`Order`, and the validation.\n- `src/core/events.ts`: the `channel` field on `OrderPlaced`.\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`: stop reading `channel` from the request.\n- Tests (`order.test.ts`, `app.test.ts`, `adapters.test.ts`, `helpers.ts`), the sample in `verify-contracts.mjs`, and the README/CLAUDE.md examples.\n\n**How would you like to go ahead?**\n1. **Confirm analytics-ingest has stopped using it.** If they've moved off `channel`, their contract file should be updated first (by them or with their sign-off). Then I can make the full removal and the contract check will pass.\n2. **Remove it from the order model only and keep it on the event.** This doesn't really work, because the event's `channel` comes from the order. Keeping it would mean keeping the input field anyway.\n3. **Go ahead anyway.** I'd make the change knowing it breaks the analytics-ingest contract. I don't recommend this without talking to that team.\n\nDo you know whether analytics-ingest has dropped `channel`, or is that contract file out of date?",
